1]Explain indetail about MultiThreading ?

	->Multithreading is a programming technique,where multiple threads are executed concurrently with in a 
	single process is called as multithreading.
	->Thread is the smallest unit of a program that can execute independently allowing multitasking and efficient
	utilization of a CPU
	
	->Key Features of MultiThreading:-
		
		i)Concurrent Execution
			->Multiple threads runs simultaneosuly improving the application performance
		
		ii)Light Weight
			->Threads within the same process share the same memory space making them less resource intensive
			than seperate processes
			
		iii)Independent
			->Threads operate independently,if one thread encounters an issue another continue running
			
			
	->Advantages of MultiThreading:-
		
		i)Improved Performance
			->By performing multiple tasks simultaneosly multithreading can enhance the application speed and 
			responsiveness
		
		ii)Better CPU utlization
			->Multithreading ensures that no CPU time is wasted while waiting for IO or other tasks
			
		iii)Better Resource sharing
			->Threads share memory and resource reducing the overhead
			
			
->In java we can create the thread in 2 ways:-
	i)By extends Thread class
	ii)By implements Runnable interface
	
->Implementing Runnable interface is most prefered way to create the Thread,because if i create the thread
by extending the Thread class i cannot extend another class in future,because java does not support multiple
inheritance,so to overcome this problem they introduced Runnable interface,and a class can implements any no
of interfaces


->Thread LifeCycle:
	->New : Thread is created,but not yet started
	->Runnable : Thread is running or it is ready to run
	->Blocked/Waiting : Thread is waiting for resource or signal
	->Teriminated : Once thread has finished its execution then the thread will be teriminated.